---
import PlaygroundShell from '../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Simulate it" hint="Two users (Alice and Bob) load the same site every 60 s through a shared CDN. You choose the response headers of each resource, then deploy a new version and see who gets stale content.">
  <ol class="how">
    <li>Run it as it starts: HTML and bundle <b>max-age=1 hour</b> (bundle name fixed), API and profile <b>max-age=5 min</b>. The deploy happens at 250 s, but Alice's HTML and bundle are <b>stale on all 5 visits</b> after it and never become fresh. Bob's profile requests return <b>Alice's data</b> (10 leaks), because the CDN stored a per-user response.</li>
    <li>Press <b>Apply recommended headers</b> (HTML <b>no-cache</b> + ETag, bundle hashed and <b>1 year immutable</b>, API <b>max-age=30, stale-while-revalidate=120</b>, profile <b>private, no-cache</b>). HTML, bundle and profile are fresh on Alice's first visit after the deploy (300 s) and there are 0 leaks. The API is stale on one visit (SWR serves the old copy once while it refreshes) and fresh at 360 s. The price: average page load rises from about 73 ms to 370 ms, because HTML and profile now cost a round trip every visit. Those answers are 304s, so the bytes stay small.</li>
    <li>Fix one thing at a time from the starting headers. Give only the <b>HTML</b> <b>no-cache + ETag</b>: the HTML is fresh at 300 s but the bundle is still stale, since its name and its cached copy did not change. Then give the <b>bundle</b> the <b>1 year immutable, hashed name</b> preset: now both are fresh. Hashing the bundle alone does nothing while the HTML pointing to it is cached.</li>
    <li>Compare <b>no-store</b> with <b>no-cache + ETag</b> on the HTML (after applying the recommended set): both are always fresh, but no-store downloads the page in full every visit (Alice's total goes from 908 KB to 1153 KB), no-cache answers with a 300 B 304.</li>
    <li>With the starting headers, set <b>Alice reloads</b> to <b>F5</b>: the HTML is refreshed (fresh at 300 s) but the bundle stays stale, because F5 only revalidates the page itself. <b>Hard reload</b> fixes everything for her, at the cost of re-downloading all of it every visit (about 4.5 MB instead of 0.45 MB).</li>
    <li>Tick <b>origin down for 120 s after the deploy</b> with the recommended set: the visits in that window fail (4 failed loads). Give the HTML, API and profile <b>stale-if-error 10 min</b> and the failures disappear, at the price of showing the old version for those visits.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="pg hc" data-hc>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Editing the headers of <select class="pg-in" data-res>
        <option value="html" selected>HTML page</option><option value="bundle">CSS/JS bundle</option><option value="api">API response</option><option value="profile">User profile</option>
      </select></label>
      <label>Preset <select class="pg-in" data-preset></select></label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>max-age <select class="pg-in" data-max></select></label>
      <label>s-maxage (CDN) <select class="pg-in" data-smax></select></label>
      <label>stale-while-revalidate <select class="pg-in" data-swr></select></label>
      <label>stale-if-error <select class="pg-in" data-sie></select></label>
      <label>Validators <select class="pg-in" data-val>
        <option value="none">none</option><option value="etag" selected>ETag</option><option value="lm">Last-Modified</option><option value="both">ETag + Last-Modified</option>
      </select></label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-row hc-checks">
      <label class="hc-check"><input type="checkbox" data-nocache /> no-cache</label>
      <label class="hc-check"><input type="checkbox" data-nostore /> no-store</label>
      <label class="hc-check"><input type="checkbox" data-priv /> private</label>
      <label class="hc-check"><input type="checkbox" data-imm /> immutable</label>
      <label class="hc-check"><input type="checkbox" data-hashed /> content-hashed file name (bundle only)</label>
    </div>
    <pre class="pg-code" data-hdrs tabindex="0" aria-label="Response headers of all four resources"></pre>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Deploy at <input type="range" class="pg-in" min="60" max="540" step="10" value="250" data-deploy /> <b data-deployval>250</b> s</label>
      <label>Alice reloads <select class="pg-in" data-reload>
        <option value="nav" selected>normal navigation</option><option value="f5">F5 (normal reload)</option><option value="hard">hard reload (Ctrl+Shift+R)</option>
      </select></label>
      <label class="hc-check"><input type="checkbox" data-outage /> origin down for 120 s after the deploy</label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <button class="btn pg-primary" type="button" data-recommend>Apply recommended headers</button>
      <button class="btn" type="button" data-reset>Reset to the starting headers</button>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-grid" aria-live="polite">
      <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--role-1)"><h3>After the deploy (Alice)</h3><span class="pg-mono hc-pre" data-fresh></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--role-3)"><h3>Cost</h3><span class="pg-mono hc-pre" data-cost></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-safebox style="--c: var(--border)"><h3>Safety</h3><span class="pg-mono hc-pre" data-safe></span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="hc-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Request timeline for Alice and Bob, one row per page visit">
      <table class="hc-table">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Time</th><th scope="col">User</th><th scope="col">HTML</th><th scope="col">Bundle</th><th scope="col">API</th><th scope="col">Profile</th><th scope="col">Page load</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody data-body></tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="pg-note">Legend: <b>browser</b> = served from the browser cache, no request; <b>304 CDN</b> = browser revalidated and the CDN answered; <b>304 origin</b> = the request reached the origin; <b>200 CDN</b> = full body from the CDN cache; <b>200 CDN (rev.)</b> = the CDN revalidated with the origin (304) then sent the body; <b>200 origin</b> = full fetch; <b>stale</b> in a cell means the version delivered was older than the origin's at that moment.</p>
    <p class="pg-note">Assumptions: 20 page visits in 10 minutes (Alice at 0, 60, 120 s ..., Bob at 30, 90 s ...); the deploy changes all four resources to v2 (the user edits the profile) at the chosen time; sizes 30 KB HTML, 400 KB bundle, 6 KB API, 2 KB profile; headers 400 B (200) or 300 B (304); browser to CDN 30 ms at 2.5 MB/s; CDN to origin 100 ms at 10 MB/s plus 5 to 60 ms of origin work; the CDN keys its cache on the URL only (no Vary: Cookie, which would be wrong anyway); heuristic freshness is 10 % of the age of Last-Modified, here 10 days. Page load = HTML, then the slowest of the other three. The background refresh of stale-while-revalidate costs bytes and origin requests but no waiting.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<script>
  import { query } from '../playground';
  // ---- core ----
  type Validator = 'none' | 'etag' | 'lm' | 'both';
  interface Cfg { max: number | null; smax: number | null; noCache: boolean; noStore: boolean; priv: boolean; immutable: boolean; swr: number; sie: number; validator: Validator; hashed: boolean }
  type Res = 'html' | 'bundle' | 'api' | 'profile';
  const RES: Res[] = ['html', 'bundle', 'api', 'profile'];
  const SIZE: Record<Res, number[]> = { html: [30000, 31000], bundle: [400000, 420000], api: [6000, 6200], profile: [2000, 2100] };
  const PROC: Record<Res, number> = { html: 40, bundle: 5, api: 60, profile: 50 };
  const HDR200 = 400; const HDR304 = 300; const RTT_U = 30; const RTT_O = 100; const BW_U = 2500; const BW_O = 10000;
  const HOUR = 3600, DAY = 24 * HOUR, YEAR = 365 * DAY; // seconds
  const LM_HEURISTIC = 0.1; // heuristic freshness: 10% of the time since Last-Modified
  const ERR_BYTES = 200; // size of an error response
  const LM_OLD = -864000; const OUTAGE_LEN = 120; const WINDOW = 600; const GAP = 60;
  const BLANK: Cfg = { max: null, smax: null, noCache: false, noStore: false, priv: false, immutable: false, swr: 0, sie: 0, validator: 'etag', hashed: false };
  const START: Record<Res, Cfg> = {
    html: { ...BLANK, max: 3600 }, bundle: { ...BLANK, max: 3600 }, api: { ...BLANK, max: 300 }, profile: { ...BLANK, max: 300 },
  };
  const RECOMMENDED: Record<Res, Cfg> = {
    html: { ...BLANK, noCache: true },
    bundle: { ...BLANK, max: YEAR, immutable: true, hashed: true },
    api: { ...BLANK, max: 30, swr: 120 },
    profile: { ...BLANK, priv: true, noCache: true },
  };
  interface Resp { res: Res; url: string; ver: number; user: string | null; bytes: number; tok: string | null; cc: Cfg; date: number; lastMod: number }
  interface Entry { resp: Resp; storedAt: number; age0: number }
  interface Store { [url: string]: Entry }
  interface Sim { cfg: Record<Res, Cfg>; deploy: number; outage: boolean; reload: 'nav' | 'f5' | 'hard' }
  interface Tot { originReqs: number; originBytes: number }
  interface UpRes { code: number; resp: Resp | null; age: number; ck: string; oMs: number }
  interface Cell { res: Res; ok: boolean; skipped: boolean; bk: string; ck: string; code: number; ver: number; stale: boolean; leak: boolean; bytes: number; ms: number; label: string }
  interface Row { t: number; user: string; cells: Cell[]; pageMs: number }

  const hasLM = (c: Cfg) => c.validator === 'lm' || c.validator === 'both';
  const hasTok = (c: Cfg) => c.validator !== 'none';
  const curAge = (e: Entry, now: number) => e.age0 + (now - e.storedAt);
  function lifetime(e: Entry, shared: boolean): number {
    const r = e.resp; const c = r.cc;
    if (c.noCache) return 0;
    if (shared && c.smax !== null) return c.smax;
    if (c.max !== null) return c.max;
    if (hasLM(c)) return Math.floor((r.date - r.lastMod) * LM_HEURISTIC); // heuristic freshness
    return 0;
  }
  const storable = (c: Cfg, shared: boolean) => !c.noStore && !(shared && c.priv);

  function originGet(S: Sim, tot: Tot, user: string, res: Res, url: string, now: number, cond: string | null): { code: number; resp: Resp | null } {
    tot.originReqs++;
    if (S.outage && now >= S.deploy && now < S.deploy + OUTAGE_LEN) return { code: 0, resp: null };
    const ver = url === 'bundle-v1' ? 1 : url === 'bundle-v2' ? 2 : now >= S.deploy ? 2 : 1;
    const c = S.cfg[res]; const who = res === 'profile' ? user : null;
    const tok = hasTok(c) ? `${url}|${who ?? '-'}|${ver}` : null;
    const resp: Resp = { res, url, ver, user: who, bytes: SIZE[res][ver - 1], tok, cc: c, date: now, lastMod: ver === 1 ? LM_OLD : S.deploy };
    if (cond !== null && tok !== null && cond === tok) return { code: 304, resp };
    tot.originBytes += HDR200 + resp.bytes;
    return { code: 200, resp };
  }
  const oLatency = (res: Res, code: number, resp: Resp | null) => RTT_O + PROC[res] + (code === 200 && resp ? (HDR200 + resp.bytes) / BW_O : 0);

  function cdnGet(S: Sim, cdn: Store, tot: Tot, user: string, res: Res, url: string, now: number, cond: string | null, mode: string): UpRes {
    const e = cdn[url];
    const answer = (resp: Resp, age: number, ck: string, oMs: number): UpRes => ({ code: cond !== null && resp.tok === cond ? 304 : 200, resp, age, ck, oMs });
    let age = 0; let life = 0;
    if (e) {
      age = curAge(e, now); life = lifetime(e, true);
      const c = e.resp.cc; const force = mode !== 'normal';
      if (!force && !c.noCache && age < life) return answer(e.resp, age, 'hit', 0);
      if (!force && !c.noCache && c.swr > 0 && age < life + c.swr) {
        const o = originGet(S, tot, user, res, url, now, e.resp.tok); // background refresh
        if (o.code === 304 && o.resp) cdn[url] = { resp: { ...e.resp, date: now }, storedAt: now, age0: 0 };
        else if (o.code === 200 && o.resp && storable(o.resp.cc, true)) cdn[url] = { resp: o.resp, storedAt: now, age0: 0 };
        return answer(e.resp, age, 'swr', 0);
      }
    }
    const o = originGet(S, tot, user, res, url, now, e ? e.resp.tok : cond);
    if (o.code === 0) {
      if (e && mode === 'normal' && age < life + e.resp.cc.sie) return answer(e.resp, age, 'stale-err', RTT_O);
      return { code: 0, resp: null, age: 0, ck: 'error', oMs: RTT_O };
    }
    const oMs = oLatency(res, o.code, o.resp);
    const r = o.resp as Resp;
    if (o.code === 304) {
      if (e) { cdn[url] = { resp: { ...e.resp, date: now }, storedAt: now, age0: 0 }; return answer(e.resp, 0, 'reval', oMs); }
      return { code: 304, resp: r, age: 0, ck: 'pass', oMs }; // not cached here: relay the origin's 304
    }
    if (storable(r.cc, true)) { cdn[url] = { resp: r, storedAt: now, age0: 0 }; return answer(r, 0, 'fetch', oMs); }
    delete cdn[url];
    return answer(r, 0, 'pass', oMs);
  }

  interface BRes { bk: string; code: number; resp: Resp | null; ck: string; bytes: number; ms: number }
  function browserGet(S: Sim, B: Store, cdn: Store, tot: Tot, user: string, res: Res, url: string, now: number, mode: string): BRes {
    const e = B[url];
    let age = 0; let life = 0;
    const network = (bg: boolean, cond: string | null): UpRes & { bytes: number; ms: number } => {
      const r = cdnGet(S, cdn, tot, user, res, url, now, cond, mode);
      const bytes = r.code === 200 && r.resp ? HDR200 + r.resp.bytes : r.code === 304 ? HDR304 : ERR_BYTES;
      const ms = RTT_U + r.oMs + (r.code === 200 && r.resp ? bytes / BW_U : 0);
      if (r.code === 304 && e) B[url] = { resp: { ...e.resp, date: now }, storedAt: now, age0: r.age };
      else if (r.code === 304 && r.resp) { /* nothing to refresh */ }
      else if (r.code === 200 && r.resp) { if (storable(r.resp.cc, false)) B[url] = { resp: r.resp, storedAt: now, age0: r.age }; else delete B[url]; }
      return { ...r, bytes, ms: bg ? 0 : ms };
    };
    if (e) {
      age = curAge(e, now); life = lifetime(e, false); const c = e.resp.cc;
      const force = mode === 'bypass' || (mode === 'revalidate' && !(c.immutable && age < life));
      if (!force && !c.noCache && age < life) return { bk: 'hit', code: 200, resp: e.resp, ck: '', bytes: 0, ms: 1 };
      if (!force && !c.noCache && c.swr > 0 && age < life + c.swr) {
        const n = network(true, e.resp.tok); const stale = e.resp;
        return { bk: 'swr', code: 200, resp: stale, ck: '', bytes: n.bytes, ms: 1 };
      }
    }
    const cond = e && mode !== 'bypass' ? e.resp.tok : null;
    const n = network(false, cond);
    if (n.code === 0) {
      if (e && mode === 'normal' && age < life + e.resp.cc.sie) return { bk: 'stale-err', code: 200, resp: e.resp, ck: n.ck, bytes: n.bytes, ms: n.ms };
      return { bk: 'error', code: 0, resp: null, ck: n.ck, bytes: n.bytes, ms: n.ms };
    }
    if (n.code === 304) return { bk: 'net', code: 304, resp: e ? e.resp : n.resp, ck: n.ck, bytes: n.bytes, ms: n.ms };
    return { bk: 'net', code: 200, resp: n.resp, ck: n.ck, bytes: n.bytes, ms: n.ms };
  }

  function label(b: BRes): string {
    if (b.bk === 'hit') return 'browser';
    if (b.bk === 'swr') return 'browser (stale, refreshing)';
    if (b.bk === 'stale-err') return 'browser (stale, origin down)';
    if (b.bk === 'error') return 'ERROR (origin down)';
    const where = b.ck === 'hit' ? 'CDN' : b.ck === 'swr' ? 'CDN (stale)' : b.ck === 'stale-err' ? 'CDN (stale, origin down)' : b.ck === 'reval' ? (b.code === 304 ? 'origin' : 'CDN (rev.)') : 'origin';
    return `${b.code} ${where}`;
  }

  function simulate(S: Sim) {
    const browsers: Store[] = [{}, {}]; const cdn: Store = {}; const tot: Tot = { originReqs: 0, originBytes: 0 };
    const events: { t: number; user: string; bi: number }[] = [];
    for (let i = 0; i < WINDOW / GAP; i++) { events.push({ t: i * GAP, user: 'Alice', bi: 0 }); events.push({ t: GAP / 2 + i * GAP, user: 'Bob', bi: 1 }); }
    events.sort((a, b) => a.t - b.t);
    const rows: Row[] = [];
    for (const ev of events) {
      const reload = ev.user === 'Alice' ? S.reload : 'nav';
      const htmlMode = reload === 'nav' ? 'normal' : reload === 'f5' ? 'revalidate' : 'bypass';
      const subMode = reload === 'hard' ? 'bypass' : 'normal';
      const cur = ev.t >= S.deploy ? 2 : 1;
      const make = (res: Res, b: BRes): Cell => {
        const ok = b.resp !== null && b.code !== 0;
        const ver = ok && b.resp ? b.resp.ver : 0;
        const stale = ok && ver < cur;
        const leak = ok && res === 'profile' && b.resp !== null && b.resp.user !== ev.user;
        return { res, ok, skipped: false, bk: b.bk, ck: b.ck, code: b.code, ver, stale, leak, bytes: b.bytes, ms: b.ms, label: label(b) };
      };
      const h = browserGet(S, browsers[ev.bi], cdn, tot, ev.user, 'html', 'html', ev.t, htmlMode);
      const cells: Cell[] = [make('html', h)];
      let sub = 0;
      if (h.resp && h.code !== 0) {
        const bundleUrl = S.cfg.bundle.hashed ? `bundle-v${h.resp.ver}` : 'bundle';
        const urls: [Res, string][] = [['bundle', bundleUrl], ['api', 'api'], ['profile', 'profile']];
        for (const [res, url] of urls) { const b = browserGet(S, browsers[ev.bi], cdn, tot, ev.user, res, url, ev.t, subMode); cells.push(make(res, b)); sub = Math.max(sub, b.ms); }
      } else {
        for (const res of ['bundle', 'api', 'profile'] as Res[]) cells.push({ res, ok: false, skipped: true, bk: 'skip', ck: '', code: 0, ver: 0, stale: false, leak: false, bytes: 0, ms: 0, label: 'not loaded' });
      }
      rows.push({ t: ev.t, user: ev.user, cells, pageMs: h.ms + sub });
    }
    // summaries
    const alice = rows.filter((r) => r.user === 'Alice');
    const post = alice.filter((r) => r.t >= S.deploy);
    const fresh = RES.map((res, i) => {
      const cs = post.map((r) => ({ t: r.t, c: r.cells[i] }));
      const stale = cs.filter((x) => x.c.stale).length;
      const first = cs.find((x) => x.c.ok && !x.c.stale);
      const failed = cs.filter((x) => !x.c.ok).length;
      return { res, visits: cs.length, stale, failed, freshAt: first ? first.t : null, lag: first ? first.t - S.deploy : null };
    });
    const leaks = rows.reduce((n, r) => n + r.cells.filter((c) => c.leak).length, 0);
    const errors = rows.reduce((n, r) => n + r.cells.filter((c) => c.bk === 'error').length, 0);
    const bytes = alice.reduce((n, r) => n + r.cells.reduce((m, c) => m + c.bytes, 0), 0);
    const avgMs = alice.reduce((n, r) => n + r.pageMs, 0) / alice.length;
    return { rows, fresh, leaks, errors, bytes, avgMs, originReqs: tot.originReqs, originBytes: tot.originBytes, total: rows.length * RES.length };
  }

  function headerLines(res: Res, c: Cfg): string {
    const p: string[] = [];
    if (c.priv) p.push('private');
    if (c.max !== null) p.push(`max-age=${c.max}`);
    if (c.smax !== null) p.push(`s-maxage=${c.smax}`);
    if (c.noCache) p.push('no-cache');
    if (c.noStore) p.push('no-store');
    if (c.immutable) p.push('immutable');
    if (c.swr > 0) p.push(`stale-while-revalidate=${c.swr}`);
    if (c.sie > 0) p.push(`stale-if-error=${c.sie}`);
    const name = res === 'bundle' ? (c.hashed ? 'app.3f9a1c.js' : 'app.js') : res === 'html' ? '/index.html' : res === 'api' ? '/api/products' : '/api/me';
    const l = [`${name}  Cache-Control: ${p.length ? p.join(', ') : '(none)'}`];
    const v = c.validator;
    if (v === 'etag' || v === 'both') l.push('    ETag: "v1"');
    if (v === 'lm' || v === 'both') l.push('    Last-Modified: 10 days ago');
    return l.join('\n');
  }
  // ---- end core ----

  const MAXS: [string, string][] = [['', '(not set)'], ['0', '0'], ['10', '10 s'], ['30', '30 s'], ['60', '60 s'], ['300', '5 min'], ['3600', '1 hour'], ['86400', '1 day'], ['31536000', '1 year']];
  const SWRS: [string, string][] = [['0', 'off'], ['30', '30 s'], ['120', '120 s'], ['600', '10 min']];
  const SIES: [string, string][] = [['0', 'off'], ['600', '10 min'], ['86400', '1 day']];
  const PRESETS: [string, string, Partial<Cfg>][] = [
    ['custom', 'Custom', {}],
    ['heur', 'No Cache-Control (heuristic freshness)', { validator: 'both' }],
    ['nostore', 'no-store', { noStore: true, validator: 'none' }],
    ['nocache', 'no-cache + ETag (revalidate every time)', { noCache: true }],
    ['short', 'max-age=60 + ETag', { max: 60 }],
    ['swr', 'max-age=30, stale-while-revalidate=120', { max: 30, swr: 120 }],
    ['sie', 'max-age=60, stale-if-error=600', { max: 60, sie: 600 }],
    ['cdn', 'max-age=0, s-maxage=300 (CDN only)', { max: 0, smax: 300 }],
    ['priv', 'private, max-age=60', { priv: true, max: 60 }],
    ['privnc', 'private, no-cache + ETag', { priv: true, noCache: true }],
    ['imm', 'max-age=1 year, immutable, hashed name', { max: YEAR, immutable: true, hashed: true }],
  ];

  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-hc]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = query(root);
    const cfg: Record<Res, Cfg> = { html: { ...START.html }, bundle: { ...START.bundle }, api: { ...START.api }, profile: { ...START.profile } };
    const presetOf: Record<Res, string> = { html: 'custom', bundle: 'custom', api: 'custom', profile: 'custom' };
    const fill = (sel: HTMLSelectElement, opts: [string, string][]) => { opts.forEach(([v, l]) => { const o = document.createElement('option'); o.value = v; o.textContent = l; sel.appendChild(o); }); };
    fill(q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-max]'), MAXS); fill(q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-smax]'), MAXS);
    fill(q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-swr]'), SWRS); fill(q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-sie]'), SIES);
    fill(q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-preset]'), PRESETS.map(([id, l]) => [id, l] as [string, string]));
    const body = q<HTMLElement>('[data-body]');
    const deployRow = document.createElement('tr'); deployRow.className = 'hc-deploy';
    const dtd = document.createElement('td'); dtd.colSpan = 7; deployRow.appendChild(dtd);
    interface RowDom { tr: HTMLElement; time: HTMLElement; user: HTMLElement; cells: { td: HTMLElement; main: HTMLElement; sub: HTMLElement }[]; page: HTMLElement }
    const pool: RowDom[] = [];
    for (let i = 0; i < (WINDOW / GAP) * 2; i++) {
      const tr = document.createElement('tr');
      const th = document.createElement('th'); th.scope = 'row'; tr.appendChild(th);
      const ut = document.createElement('td'); tr.appendChild(ut);
      const cells = RES.map(() => {
        const td = document.createElement('td'); const main = document.createElement('span'); main.className = 'hc-main'; const sub = document.createElement('span'); sub.className = 'hc-sub';
        td.append(main, sub); tr.appendChild(td); return { td, main, sub };
      });
      const page = document.createElement('td'); tr.appendChild(page);
      pool.push({ tr, time: th, user: ut, cells, page });
    }

    const cur = () => q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-res]').value as Res;
    function syncControls() {
      const r = cur(); const c = cfg[r];
      q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-max]').value = c.max === null ? '' : String(c.max);
      q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-smax]').value = c.smax === null ? '' : String(c.smax);
      q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-swr]').value = String(c.swr);
      q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-sie]').value = String(c.sie);
      q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-val]').value = c.validator;
      q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-nocache]').checked = c.noCache;
      q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-nostore]').checked = c.noStore;
      q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-priv]').checked = c.priv;
      q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-imm]').checked = c.immutable;
      const h = q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-hashed]'); h.checked = r === 'bundle' && c.hashed; h.disabled = r !== 'bundle';
      q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-preset]').value = presetOf[r];
    }
    function readControls() {
      const r = cur(); const c = cfg[r];
      const mv = q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-max]').value; const sv = q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-smax]').value;
      c.max = mv === '' ? null : Number(mv); c.smax = sv === '' ? null : Number(sv);
      c.swr = Number(q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-swr]').value); c.sie = Number(q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-sie]').value);
      c.validator = q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-val]').value as Validator;
      c.noCache = q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-nocache]').checked; c.noStore = q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-nostore]').checked;
      c.priv = q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-priv]').checked; c.immutable = q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-imm]').checked;
      c.hashed = r === 'bundle' && q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-hashed]').checked;
    }
    const sec = (n: number) => (n >= DAY ? `${Math.round(n / HOUR)} h` : `${n} s`);
    function render() {
      const S: Sim = { cfg, deploy: Number(q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-deploy]').value), outage: q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-outage]').checked, reload: q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-reload]').value as Sim['reload'] };
      q('[data-deployval]').textContent = String(S.deploy);
      q('[data-hdrs]').textContent = RES.map((r) => headerLines(r, cfg[r])).join('\n');
      const out = simulate(S);
      const names: Record<Res, string> = { html: 'HTML', bundle: 'Bundle', api: 'API', profile: 'Profile' };
      q('[data-fresh]').textContent = out.fresh.map((f) => {
        if (f.visits === 0) return `${names[f.res]}: no visit after the deploy`;
        if (f.freshAt === null) return `${names[f.res]}: never fresh (${f.stale} stale, ${f.failed} failed, of ${f.visits} visit${f.visits === 1 ? '' : 's'})`;
        if (f.stale === 0) return `${names[f.res]}: fresh at once (t=${f.freshAt} s)`;
        return `${names[f.res]}: stale on ${f.stale} of ${f.visits} visit${f.visits === 1 ? '' : 's'}, fresh at t=${f.freshAt} s (+${f.lag} s)`;
      }).join('\n');
      q('[data-cost]').textContent = `Alice page load: ${Math.round(out.avgMs)} ms on average\nAlice downloaded: ${(out.bytes / 1000).toFixed(1)} KB\nOrigin requests: ${out.originReqs} (${out.total} resource loads)\nOrigin bytes sent: ${(out.originBytes / 1000).toFixed(1)} KB`;
      q('[data-safe]').textContent = `Wrong user's profile served: ${out.leaks}\nFailed loads: ${out.errors}`;
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-safebox]').style.setProperty('--c', out.leaks > 0 || out.errors > 0 ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--role-3)');
      dtd.textContent = `Deploy at t=${S.deploy} s: HTML, bundle, API and profile are now v2${S.outage ? `; origin down until t=${S.deploy + OUTAGE_LEN} s` : ''}`;
      let placed = false;
      const frag: HTMLElement[] = [];
      out.rows.forEach((row, i) => {
        if (!placed && S.deploy <= row.t) { frag.push(deployRow); placed = true; }
        const d = pool[i];
        d.time.textContent = `${row.t} s`; d.user.textContent = row.user; d.tr.className = row.user === 'Bob' ? 'hc-bob' : '';
        row.cells.forEach((c, k) => {
          const cd = d.cells[k];
          const kind = c.skipped ? 'skip' : c.bk === 'hit' ? 'browser' : c.bk === 'swr' || c.bk === 'stale-err' ? 'swr' : c.bk === 'error' ? 'err' : c.code === 304 ? 'r304' : c.ck === 'hit' || c.ck === 'swr' || c.ck === 'stale-err' ? 'cdn' : 'origin';
          cd.td.className = `hc-c hc-${kind}${c.stale ? ' hc-stale' : ''}${c.leak ? ' hc-leak' : ''}`;
          cd.main.textContent = c.label + (c.leak ? ' LEAK' : '');
          cd.sub.textContent = c.skipped ? '' : `v${c.ver || '?'}${c.stale ? ' stale' : ''}${c.leak ? ' (not yours)' : ''} · ${c.bytes ? (c.bytes / 1000).toFixed(1) + ' KB' : '0 B'} · ${Math.round(c.ms)} ms`;
        });
        d.page.textContent = `${Math.round(row.pageMs)} ms`;
        frag.push(d.tr);
      });
      if (!placed) frag.push(deployRow);
      body.replaceChildren(...frag);
    }
    let raf = 0;
    const schedule = () => { if (raf) return; raf = requestAnimationFrame(() => { raf = 0; render(); }); };
    const custom = () => { presetOf[cur()] = 'custom'; q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-preset]').value = 'custom'; };
    ['[data-max]', '[data-smax]', '[data-swr]', '[data-sie]', '[data-val]', '[data-nocache]', '[data-nostore]', '[data-priv]', '[data-imm]', '[data-hashed]'].forEach((s) => {
      q(s).addEventListener('change', () => { readControls(); custom(); schedule(); });
    });
    q('[data-res]').addEventListener('change', () => { syncControls(); });
    q('[data-preset]').addEventListener('change', () => {
      const id = q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-preset]').value; const r = cur();
      const p = PRESETS.find((x) => x[0] === id);
      if (p && id !== 'custom') { cfg[r] = { ...BLANK, ...p[2] }; if (r !== 'bundle') cfg[r].hashed = false; presetOf[r] = id; }
      syncControls(); schedule();
    });
    ['[data-deploy]', '[data-outage]', '[data-reload]'].forEach((s) => q(s).addEventListener('input', schedule));
    q('[data-recommend]').addEventListener('click', () => { RES.forEach((r) => { cfg[r] = { ...RECOMMENDED[r] }; presetOf[r] = 'custom'; }); syncControls(); schedule(); });
    q('[data-reset]').addEventListener('click', () => { RES.forEach((r) => { cfg[r] = { ...START[r] }; presetOf[r] = 'custom'; }); syncControls(); schedule(); });
    syncControls(); render();
  });
</script>
<style is:global>
  .playground .hc-check { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; }
  .playground .hc-pre { white-space: pre-wrap; }
  .playground .hc-scroll { overflow-x: auto; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px; max-height: 460px; overflow-y: auto; }
  .playground .hc-table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; min-width: 760px; font-size: .8rem; }
  .playground .hc-table th, .playground .hc-table td { padding: 4px 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); text-align: left; vertical-align: top; }
  .playground .hc-table thead th { position: sticky; top: 0; background: var(--surface-2); z-index: 1; }
  .playground .hc-table tbody th { white-space: nowrap; font-weight: 600; }
  .playground .hc-bob { background: var(--surface-2); }
  .playground .hc-deploy td { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--role-4) 18%, var(--surface)); font-weight: 600; }
  .playground .hc-c { border-left: 4px solid var(--c, var(--border)); }
  .playground .hc-browser { --c: var(--role-2); }
  .playground .hc-cdn { --c: var(--role-3); }
  .playground .hc-r304 { --c: var(--role-4); }
  .playground .hc-origin { --c: var(--role-5); }
  .playground .hc-swr { --c: var(--role-6); }
  .playground .hc-err { --c: var(--bad); }
  .playground .hc-main { display: block; font-weight: 600; }
  .playground .hc-sub { display: block; color: var(--muted); font: .74rem var(--font-mono); white-space: nowrap; }
  .playground .hc-stale .hc-sub { color: var(--bad-text); font-weight: 700; }
  .playground .hc-leak { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--bad) 14%, var(--surface)); }
  .playground .hc-leak .hc-main { color: var(--bad-text); }
</style>
